samsung has just revealed the galaxy s21  smartphone lineup  and we've already pre-ordered our top  spec ultra model  so we figured we would see exactly how  it compares to apple's iphone 12 pro max  to see if we have a new flagship  smartphone king so in this video  i'm gonna go through all the specs i'm  gonna compare all the features  and i'm gonna look at the performance of  the new snapdragon 888 chip  compared to the a14 bionic in the iphone  12 pro max  to see if the new galaxy s29 ultra is  right for you  so let's jump right into it first off it  comes with a new design that's more  rounded than before  and the camera bump looks way different  being kind of built into the frame  to me it seems like they did this  because the camera bump is so massive  looking just as big as it was on the  note 20 ultra which was much thicker  than the one on the iphone 12 pro max  they're also going  all matte this year like this new black  matte finish  and i personally really like how it  looks and it should feel really good in  the hand as well  weighing just one gram heavier than the  iphone 12 pro max  the display this year is absolutely  killer it's 6.8 inches large  so just slightly bigger than apple's 6.7  inch display  but it features a higher 3200 by 1440  resolution  the main issue we had last year with the  s20 ultra  is that we had to lower the resolution  to use the 120  hertz refresh rate mode but on the s21  ultra  you get both 120 hertz and full res  at the same time and if you're worried  about battery life samsung  solved this issue by using adaptive  refresh rate  which automatically adjusts between 10  hertz and 120 hertz  depending on the content you're viewing  just like apple has been doing for years  with the pro motion tech in the ipad pro  this  is absolutely huge because you no longer  have to choose between resolution  and refresh rate while the iphone 12 pro  is still limited to 60 hertz which at  this point  is just embarrassing not only that but  the s21 ultra's display  can now reach 1500 nits while viewing  hdr content  compared to 1200 nits on the iphone so  based on all of that  the s21 ultra's display kills the  iphones  in basically every single way there's  just no competition here  as far as the battery the one on the  samsung is a much larger 5 000 milliamp  hours  so it should definitely last longer than  the one on the 12 pro max  even with 120hz mode enabled which is  very impressive  the s21 ultra will come with 128 gigs of  storage  and 12 gigs of ram at the base price  which is twice as much ram  as you get on the iphone and you can  even get up to 16 gigs of ram  if you buy the maxed out 512 gig model  but as we already know iphones are very  ram  efficient so we'll have to test it out  ourselves when we finally get our hands  on the s20 ultra  so subscribe right now if you want to  see that one of the biggest drawbacks to  the s21 ultra is that they finally  ditched  the micro sd card slot which was one of  the main reasons people  bought galaxy phones in the past and  just as expected  there is no longer a charger or earbuds  in the box  which is kind of funny because samsung  mocked apple for doing this on their  iphone 12 lineup but because of that  samsung was able to get the price down  to twelve hundred dollars instead of  last year's  fourteen hundred dollars for the s20  ultra which was definitely  way too expensive and led to a drop in  sales  now before i get into comparing the  chips i want to mention a few more spec  differences and features  as expected the s21 ultra gets both sub  6  and millimeter wave 5g but something new  this year is an  ultra wide band radio chip which apple  already introduced with the iphone 11  pro along with that they released their  new galaxy tags  which can be used to track devices and  items like your keys  and as we already know apple has had  their own version in the works for over  a year now  but it's still not released and this  ultra wideband chip will also give you  more features like using your phone  as your car key and samsung already  partnered with audi  bmw ford and genesis to get this feature  up and running on new cars  one major new feature is the addition of  wi-fi 6e  which is unique because it uses a brand  new frequency band  compared to wi-fi 6 on the iphone which  uses the existing bands  so keep in mind that you're going to  need a new wi-fi 6e router  if you want to take advantage of this  samsung is also for the first time  adding s pen support to the s21 ultra  so you no longer need to wait for the  note model if you really want that pen  but this time it doesn't fit into the  phone itself  so it doesn't have a little spring  loaded button on the bottom instead  samsung is selling a couple of cases  that have a slot to hold the s pen  but this can be an issue because the  case is gonna make it even more wide and  large  and some people just don't like using a  case the s pen isn't included in the box  it's actually a forty dollar purchase by  itself or you can get it bundled with a  case  for seventy dollars which isn't that bad  of a deal  and as we know the iphone still doesn't  support any type of stylus  probably because apple wants you to buy  an ipad on the side  to use the apple pencil and one more  thing the s21 ultra features qualcomm's  brand new under display fingerprint  sensor which is 1.77 times larger than  the previous one  and it should be faster as well this is  actually crazy because even the  old version was faster than face id with  the only issue being reliability  so the larger size should definitely  help with that  and we're really excited to test it out  again now let's finally get into  performance and compare the new  snapdragon  888 chip to apple's a14 bionic  in geekbench 5 the iphone is a massive  40  faster in terms of single core  performance which is gonna make it feel  very snappy for common tasks and in  multi-core the iphone is still around  nine percent faster  even with only six gigs of slower lp  ddr4x ram  compared to 12 gigs of lp ddr5 ram  on the samsung so it looks like the  snapdragon is still a bit behind  but it's still extremely fast with that  let's finally get into the cameras and  there are a ton of changes this year  with the s21 ultra it now has five  cameras total  including a 40 megapixel selfie camera  that destroys  the 12 megapixel selfie cam on the  iphone 12 pro max  just like it did before the main camera  on the s21 ultra still uses a 108  megapixel sensor  which utilizes binning if you don't want  to use that mode but a major difference  this year is the fact that it now uses a  laser autofocus system  which is extremely important because the  absolute biggest issue with last year's  s20 ultra  was major auto focusing problems laser  autofocus should now fix that  and according to unbox therapy's video  even the 8k  24 fps video mode utilizes this  so thankfully we can now finally use  this mode without having auto focus  issues  but it still looks like the optical  image stabilization  is turned off in this mode they've also  got a really handy video recording  feature this year  director's view which allows you to view  and switch between angles  on the fly while on the iphone you can't  even switch  from the rear camera to the selfie cam  while recording and now  the s21 ultra can finally record 4k  60fps video  on any of the four cameras just like the  iphone can  which was a big drawback last year with  the s20 ultra  and as far as the ultrawide camera it  features a 12 megapixel sensor  just like the one you get with the  iphone and now the s21 ultra has not one  but two telephoto cameras both with 10  megapixel sensors  with one of them being an optical 3x  zoom  with the other being an optical 10x zoom  this is actually a really good idea  because the 3x camera features a decent  f 2.4 aperture letting in a bunch of  light  while the 10x zoom has a really bad  f 4.9 aperture so it should only be used  exclusively for long range zoom shots  when you really need it now i don't know  if you know this  but last year's s20 ultra only actually  had  a 4x optical zoom lens even though they  advertised the crazy 100x space zoom  so the s21 should do a much better job  and it should absolutely smoke  the iphone 12 pro max which only has a  single  2.5 x telephoto lens so in terms of the  cameras  i honestly believe that the s21 ultra  will now smoke the iphone 12 pro max  in terms of camera quality no questions  asked  but of course we're gonna have to see  when we compare them later this month  when it gets released on the 29th so  with all of that  said i've got to say that at just a  hundred dollars more expensive  than the 12 pro max the new s21 ultra is  gonna be  the better flagship phone even if the  performance doesn't quite match up  the main drawback this year is the lack  of a micro sd card slot  so if that's a big deal for you let me  know down in the comment section below  and if you want to see our full  comparison and camera test videos  click that circle above to subscribe so  you don't miss out on that and be sure  to watch one of those two videos right  over there thanks for watching and we'll  see you in the next video
 

